00","id":182456,"title":"","content":"I love my blue-hardback copy of Aberrant. Shiny gold print, with Randall about to change the world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T05:41:43-07:00","id":188657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=182128#post182128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very much so, and probably intentional. Aberrant never really goes out of its way to hide its pedigree.<br /> <br /> As a setting, Aberrant is descended from a tradition of deconstructionist superhero stories. Other sources that could be noted would be the Authority, Dark Knight Returns, Marvelman, Planetary and Watchmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the mean time, we've had lots more like Supergod, Uber and so on. I am very glad that OPP is embracing this rich history rather than ostensibly turning away from it as the infamous sidebar did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:49:34-07:00","id":188783,"title":"","content":"Warren Ellis is basically a giant virus that's infected the Trinity DNA with his heinous disease. We could try to burn him out, but at this point it's more animal than man. If you look closely you'll see a lot of Planetary, Global Frequency and newuniversal in Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:28:21-07:00","id":188824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188657#post188657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as the infamous sidebar did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidebar? Sorry, I've been busy lately, so I haven't been able to read all the books I've wanted. Which sidebar?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T13:29:31-07:00","id":188902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188783#post188783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warren Ellis is basically a giant virus that's infected the Trinity DNA with his heinous disease. We could try to burn him out, but at this point it's more animal than man. If you look closely you'll see a lot of Planetary, Global Frequency and newuniversal in Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh yeah, New Universal. Which sadly was never finished, though Hickman is bringing into his (excellent) Avengers run","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T13:30:58-07:00","id":188905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188824#post188824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidebar? Sorry, I've been busy lately, so I haven't been able to read all the books I've wanted. Which sidebar?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a sidebar in the Aberrant core book (I think? Been a while!) about how this isn't the Justice Friends leave your grandad's superheroes at home and really it was a bit ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T13:46:14-07:00","id":188909,"title":"","content":"Hm, didn't see that one. Yeah, this game came out back at the tail end of the &quot;deconstruction&quot; craze, didn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:41:47-07:00","id":188933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188905#post188905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was a sidebar in the Aberrant core book (I think? Been a while!) about how this isn't the Justice Friends leave your grandad's superheroes at home and really it was a bit ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite.<br /> <br /> The introduction/essay to the Aberrant Players Guide was titled &quot;This is Not Superfriends.&quot; The APG was the final printed product in the Aberrant line, followed only by Underworld, which was one of White Wolf's first PDF products. Despite coming in at the tail end of the line, it's sort of cast a shadow over all of Aberrant.<br /> <br /> I can't say what Kraig intended with that particular introduction -- I haven't spoken to him about it -- but I don't really agree with it as it's commonly understood. As I see it, my job is to present you with a framework. That framework will explicitly support the game we've written about, but if it's solid and robust enough to support other stuff too? Bonus. Do you want to kitbash it to run a literal Avengers or Superfriends game? Great. To the question &quot;am I playing this game right,&quot; the only answer I care about is the same as the answer to the question &quot;are you having fun playing it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:44:21-07:00","id":188935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188783#post188783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warren Ellis is basically a giant virus that's infected the Trinity DNA with his heinous disease. We could try to burn him out, but at this point it's more animal than man. If you look closely you'll see a lot of Planetary, Global Frequency and newuniversal in Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I maintain it's no coincidence that Michael Donighal was born in 1900.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T15:34:25-07:00","id":188947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=188933#post188933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite.<br /> <br /> The introduction/essay to the Aberrant Players Guide was titled &quot;This is Not Superfriends.&quot; The APG was the final printed product in the Aberrant line, followed only by Underworld, which was one of White Wolf's first PDF products. Despite coming in at the tail end of the line, it's sort of cast a shadow over all of Aberrant.<br /> <br /> I can't say what Kraig intended with that particular introduction -- I haven't spoken to him about it -- but I don't really agree with it as it's commonly understood. As I see it, my job is to present you with a framework. That framework will explicitly support the game we've written about, but if it's solid and robust enough to support other stuff too? Bonus. Do you want to kitbash it to run a literal Avengers or Superfriends game? Great. To the question &quot;am I playing this game right,&quot; the only answer I care about is the same as the answer to the question &quot;are you having fun playing it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I was remembering the wrong book, but couldn't remember where it was! I definitely think that Aberrant would be pretty great for running certain styles of Marvel and DC comics. I very much expect to be able to use it for a Hickman style Avengers run, or a Morrison style JLA, or a Gillen style X-Men Extinction team. I am very glad that we're moving away from an idea that this isn't superheroes because it is, really, it's doing what a lot of superhero books are doing, and there's nothing wrong with that. There's a lot <i>right</i> with that.<br /> <br /> I am very excited for Aberrant, not just for Aberrant itself (though I am super pumped for that too) but because my go-to supers game, M&amp;M3, does pretty much everything great except those Ellis/Gillen/Hickman style modern supergods stories with a hard edge (I'm reminded of Gillen's little essay at the beginning of Uber, <i>&quot;It doesn't matter if Spider-Man's fighting Galactus \u2014 Spider-Man will find a way to beat Galactus. <b>Uber</b> isn't that story. <b>Uber</b> is the story that every single time, Galactus will kill Spider-Man.&quot;).</i> I am very confident that this style will be well and truly fulfilled by Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T23:44:09-07:00","id":189218,"title":"","content":"Heck, The final fight between Superman and Zod in Man of Steel felt like an Aberrant combat (property damage and loss of life included)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:57:10-07:00","id":189620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=189218#post189218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, The final fight between Superman and Zod in Man of Steel felt like an Aberrant combat (property damage and loss of life included)!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why'd you have to remind me? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T07:16:38-07:00","id":190250,"title":"","content":"Yeah, baselines die a whole lot when Aberrants fight. That's always great to see the look of shock on some first-time player's face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:16:09-07:00","id":190613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/182081-aberrant-and-wildcards?p=190250#post190250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, baselines die a whole lot when Aberrants fight. That's always great to see the look of shock on some first-time player's face.</div> </div> </div> </div>JMS' Squadron Supreme really rammed that home too<br /> <br /> When Doctor Spectrum and Hyperion fought there were no humans around, but a whole bunch of African Sahara wildlife bought the farm and they never even noticed they were there. When Hyperion and Redstone fight there are humans around, and Redstone is a psychopath. So there's a <i>lot</i> of deaths. I always thought that the trick to playing a proper Nova superhero wasn't being powerful (though you need that) but also being really,<i> really</i> clever and careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T02:51:40-07:00","id":191270,"title":"","content":"In a campaign I used to run, the team long-range transporter (who was called Vortex) had a hard time controlling the wormhole-like portals she produced and they would often slip a bit on one end or the other (or both). When that would happen anything going in one end would be forcefully ejected out the other which was not a problem for the flyers or even the non-flying team tank since he was used to playing human cannonball; it was considerably less fun for any baseline unlucky enough to be caught in the input end or having to try to dodge debris like dumpsters or cars on the output end or even one time the water (and fish) cannon from hell when the input end slipped into a major aquarium tank. And that kind of collateral damage was mild compared to the mess they made actually fighting someone, even with them trying to be careful.<br /> <br /> With great power comes great havoc (ever see Tank Police?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}